  "speechText": "Yes, that is true. My strongest foundation is backend engineering. That's because in production, an AI feature is not only the model. It still needs data pipelines, retrieval, APIs, queues, state, retries, monitoring, security, and infrastructure. Those are areas where I already have strong hands-on experience from building and running production backend systems. So I can grow deeper in AI without starting from zero on the production engineering side. Recently, I have also worked with OCR, embeddings, hybrid retrieval, LLM integration, model reliability, and GPU inference. That includes systems like StrangeLoop and RAG. So overall, I am building stronger AI capability on top of a solid production backend foundation.",
